classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: rate
Nonnegative Poisson arrivals/second; default 10.
argument:: decay
Exponential time constant in seconds; default 0.05. Nonpositive means instantaneous marks held for one calculation.
argument:: ampMean
Gaussian mark mean; default 0.
argument:: ampStd
Gaussian mark standard deviation by magnitude; default 1. Zero gives fixed-size marks.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local PCG32 seed. Zero derives a seed from the parent Synth; nonzero is reproducible. Reset restores the original seed.
argument:: reset
Rising edge clears signal, timing debt, and hazard schedule, and restores the seed. No event on reset.
returns:: Exactly two outputs: [signal, eventTrigger]. Signal is not normalized; trigger is binary.

method:: kr
Control-rate version: one calculation spans the full control block. Event outputs last one block.

instancemethods::

examples::

subsection:: Sparse shots

The short decay exposes individual impacts within seconds.

code::
(
{ ShotNoise.ar(12, 0.03, 0, 0.5)[0] * 0.1 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.03) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Fixed marks

Separate the arrival flag from the accumulated signal.

code::
(
{ ShotNoise.kr(5, 0.2, 1, 0, seed: 31).poll(10) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Particles into material

Increasing rate moves from separate particles to overlapping resonant texture.

code::
(
{
    var rate = SinOsc.kr(0.05).exprange(2, 180);
    var particles = ShotNoise.ar(rate, 0.006, 0, 0.4)[0];
    Splay.ar(Ringz.ar(particles, [430, 710, 1130], [0.12, 0.2, 0.28]))
        * 0.015 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::
